statement:
Fix an integer \(h\geq3\), put \(N:=h^2\), \(n:=2\), and \(d:=2N\).  Write \(\mathbb R^d=H_1\oplus H_2\), with \(H_1=H_2=\mathbb R^N\).  If \(\xi_1,\ldots,\xi_N\) is the standard basis of \(H_1\) and \(\mathbf 1:=\sum_i\xi_i\), set

\[
 u_i:=\sqrt{\frac{N}{N-1}}\left(\xi_i-\frac1N\mathbf 1\right),
 \qquad
 f_s:=\sqrt{\frac{N(s-1)}{s(N-1)}}.
\tag{1}
\]

Choose

\[
 f_h^{-1}<\alpha<f_{h-1}^{-1}.
\tag{2}
\]

Let \(\eta_1,\ldots,\eta_N\) be the standard basis of \(H_2\), put

\[
 S:=\left(N,\frac{N(N+1)}2\right),
 \qquad
 p_i:=-S+2\sum_{j=1}^{i-1}(1,j)\in\mathbb Z^2,
\tag{3}
\]

and define

\[
 c_i^+:=-\alpha u_i+\eta_i,
 \qquad
 c_i^-:=-\alpha u_i-\eta_i.
\tag{4}
\]

Let \(B_d\) be the Euclidean unit ball.  Choose \(R_d>0\) so that the half-mass metronoid of \(R_dB_d\) is \(B_d\), write

\[
 a:=\operatorname{vol}_d(R_dB_d),
\tag{5}
\]

and consider the genuine convex body

\[
 C:=\operatorname{conv}\bigcup_{i=1}^N
 \left(
 \{p_i\}\times(c_i^++R_dB_d)
 \ \cup\
 \{-p_i\}\times(c_i^-+R_dB_d)
 \right).
\tag{6}
\]

For every \(z\in\mathbb Z^2\), use the canonical notation

\[
 C_z:=\{x:(z,x)\in C\},
 \qquad
 a_z:=\operatorname{vol}_d(C_z),
 \qquad
 \mathcal K_z:=\mathsf M_{a_z/2}(C_z),
\tag{7}
\]

and put \(Z:=\{z:a_z>0\}\), \(W:=\sum_{z\in Z}a_z\), and \(G:=\mathfrak C_{\mathrm{core}}(C)\).  Assume the canonical branch \(G<W/4\), and let \(r=(r_e)\), \(Q:=\sum_er_e>0\), \(R\), \(R_{\mathrm{sel}}(C)\), \(M_{\mathrm{off}}(C)\), \(R_{\mathrm{cloud}}(C)\), and

\[
 D:=2^2h_{\max}(C)
\tag{8}
\]

have exactly the canonical meanings of accepted facts `c81f02314cb34f8b`, `6b09aae189415c70`, and `637b5f7874d8c875`.  Thus, for a good parity class \(\zeta\),

\[
 A_\zeta:=\sum_{z\equiv\zeta}a_z,
 \qquad
 r_{\{u,v\}}=\frac{a_ua_v}{4A_\zeta}
 \quad(u\ne v,\ u\equiv v\equiv\zeta),
\tag{9}
\]

while the reservoir is zero on a bad class.

Let

\[
 \mathcal E_{\mathrm{ant}}
 :=\{e_i:=\{p_i,-p_i\}:1\leq i\leq N\},
 \qquad
 q_{\mathrm{ant}}:=\sum_{e\in\mathcal E_{\mathrm{ant}}}r_e.
\tag{10}
\]

Choose the actual load-minimal optimizer of accepted fact `6496cb3b0fd44f9d` for the full canonical reservoir, not for the restricted family (10), and write

\[
 \omega_e:=h_{D_e}(v_e),
 \qquad
 \Omega:=\sum_e\omega_e,
 \qquad
 \Omega_{\mathrm{ant}}:=\sum_{e\in\mathcal E_{\mathrm{ant}}}\omega_e,
 \qquad
 \Omega_{\mathrm{comp}}:=\Omega-\Omega_{\mathrm{ant}}.
\tag{11}
\]

At the physical target \(0\), use the exact congestion normalization of accepted fact `f6188983e8850f01`:

\[
 \vartheta_e:=2^{-(d+1)}
 (a_u^{1/d}+a_v^{1/d})^d,
 \qquad
 \kappa_0:=\sum_{e:m_e=0}\frac{\omega_e}{\vartheta_e},
 \qquad
 \chi_0:=\frac1{\max\{1,\kappa_0\}}.
\tag{12}
\]

Put

\[
 \kappa_{\mathrm{ant}}
 :=\sum_{e\in\mathcal E_{\mathrm{ant}}}
 \frac{\omega_e}{\vartheta_e},
 \qquad
 \kappa_{\mathrm{comp},0}:=\kappa_0-\kappa_{\mathrm{ant}},
 \qquad
 B_{\mathrm{ant}}
 :=(1-\chi_0)\Omega_{\mathrm{ant}}.
\tag{13}
\]

Then all of the following hold.

1. Every convexity-forced positive integer fiber is included exactly: if

\[
 P:=\operatorname{conv}\{p_i,-p_i:1\leq i\leq N\},
\tag{14}
\]

then \(Z=P\cap\mathbb Z^2\).  The displayed points are exposed vertices, their fibers are exactly the translated balls in (6), and hence

\[
 a_{p_i}=a_{-p_i}=a,
 \qquad
 \mathcal K_{p_i}=c_i^++B_d,
 \qquad
 \mathcal K_{-p_i}=c_i^-+B_d.
\tag{15}
\]

All \(2N\) displayed vertices lie in one parity class, denoted \(\zeta_*\).  The sums \(A_{\zeta_*}\) and \(Q\) in (9) include every additional lattice fiber in (14), with its actual volume \(a_z\).

2. If \(\zeta_*\) is bad, then

\[
 q_{\mathrm{ant}}=\Omega_{\mathrm{ant}}
 =\kappa_{\mathrm{ant}}=B_{\mathrm{ant}}=0.
\tag{16}
\]

If \(\zeta_*\) is good, then the exact canonical weights and the all-fiber class mass give

\[
 r_{e_i}=\frac{a^2}{4A_{\zeta_*}},
 \qquad
 q_{\mathrm{ant}}
 =\frac{Na^2}{4A_{\zeta_*}}
 \leq\frac a8,
\tag{17}
\]

\[
 Q\geq Q_{\zeta_*}
 :=\frac{A_{\zeta_*}^2-
 \sum_{z\equiv\zeta_*}a_z^2}{8A_{\zeta_*}}
 \geq\frac{3A_{\zeta_*}}{32}
 \geq\frac{3Na}{16},
\tag{18}
\]

and therefore

\[
 \boxed{
 \frac{q_{\mathrm{ant}}}{Q}
 \leq\frac{2}{3N}
 =\frac{2}{3h^2}.}
\tag{19}
\]

3. The following are rigorous lower bounds for all six canonical hard-ledger capacities, and the optimizer bound is for the actual full-reservoir optimizer:

\[
 \boxed{R\geq Q-\Omega,}
\tag{20}
\]

\[
 \boxed{G\geq4a,}
 \qquad
 \boxed{R_{\mathrm{sel}}(C)\geq4\gamma_da,}
\tag{21}
\]

where \(\gamma_d=(d/(d+1))^d\).  If \(q_{\mathrm{ant}}>0\), then

\[
 \boxed{
 M_{\mathrm{off}}(C)
 \geq\frac{4q_{\mathrm{ant}}}{N},}
 \qquad
 \boxed{
 R_{\mathrm{cloud}}(C)
 \geq\frac{16\gamma_{2d}q_{\mathrm{ant}}}{N},}
\tag{22}
\]

and in every case

\[
 \boxed{
 D\geq
 \max\{4\gamma_da,
 M_{\mathrm{off}}(C),R_{\mathrm{cloud}}(C)\}.}
\tag{23}
\]

The two bounds in (22) are interpreted as zero lower bounds when \(q_{\mathrm{ant}}=0\).

4. On every antipodal edge,

\[
 m_{e_i}=0,
 \qquad
 L_{e_i}=-\alpha u_i+B_d,
 \qquad
 \vartheta_{e_i}=\frac a2.
\tag{24}
\]

The actual optimizer and target multiplier therefore satisfy

\[
 \boxed{
 0\leq\Omega_{\mathrm{ant}}
 \leq q_{\mathrm{ant}}
 \leq\frac{2Q}{3h^2},}
 \qquad
 \boxed{0\leq\kappa_{\mathrm{ant}}\leq\frac14,}
\tag{25}
\]

\[
 \boxed{
 0\leq B_{\mathrm{ant}}
 \leq\Omega_{\mathrm{ant}}
 \leq\frac{2Q}{3h^2}.}
\tag{26}
\]

If \(\chi_0<1\), then the completed target-zero edges, meaning all canonical target-zero edges outside \(\mathcal E_{\mathrm{ant}}\), satisfy

\[
 \boxed{\kappa_{\mathrm{comp},0}>\frac34.}
\tag{27}
\]

If \(\chi_0=1\), then \(B_{\mathrm{ant}}=0\).  Thus the antipodal family cannot by itself create positive-fresh target congestion.

5. The affine non-hit families among (24) are exactly the subsets of cardinality at least \(h\), and the inclusion-minimal ones are exactly the \(h\)-subsets.  For the canonical positive-fresh edge capacities

\[
 \beta_e:=(1-\chi_{m_e})\omega_e
\tag{28}
\]

of accepted facts `637b5f7874d8c875` and `fd621e3189426c0d`, let

\[
 C_{\mathrm{ant}}
 :=\max_{x\in\mathbb R^d}
 \sum_{i:x\in-\alpha u_i+B_d}\beta_{e_i}.
\tag{29}
\]

Let \(\mathsf P_{\mathrm{ant}}\) be the fractional packing of all \(h\)-subsets of \(\mathcal E_{\mathrm{ant}}\) under the vertex capacities \(\beta_e\).  Then

\[
 \boxed{
 0\leq B_{\mathrm{ant}}-C_{\mathrm{ant}}
 \leq B_{\mathrm{ant}}
 \leq\frac{2Q}{3h^2},}
\tag{30}
\]

and

\[
 \boxed{
 \mathsf P_{\mathrm{ant}}
 \leq\frac{B_{\mathrm{ant}}}{h}
 \leq\frac{2Q}{3h^3}.}
\tag{31}
\]

Every other nonnegative no-reuse charge supported on the antipodal edges and dominated edgewise by \(\beta\), including the antipodal part of a fresh load, is at most \(B_{\mathrm{ant}}\).  Hence the complete-\(h\)-uniform blocker defect and its packing are \(o(Q)\).

6. Finally, if the six-capacity canonical ledger is hard,

\[
 R+G+R_{\mathrm{sel}}(C)+M_{\mathrm{off}}(C)
 +R_{\mathrm{cloud}}(C)+D<\frac Q{100},
\tag{32}
\]

then

\[
 q_{\mathrm{ant}}
 <\min\left\{\frac{2}{3h^2},\frac1{3200}\right\}Q,
\tag{33}
\]

and the actual optimizer has

\[
 \boxed{
 \Omega_{\mathrm{comp}}
 >\left(
 \frac{99}{100}
 -\min\left\{\frac{2}{3h^2},\frac1{3200}\right\}
 \right)Q.}
\tag{34}
\]

Thus, under the hard ledger, essentially all load has certified provenance on the canonical cross-pair/interior-fiber completion, while the selected antipodal obstruction is microscopic.  This conclusion does not assert that the completed load has already been absorbed into a terminal capacity.
